process-media (2.0.1-2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * No source change. Switch ``Distribution:`` to ``unstable`` so the
    package passes ``lintian --check changes``; ``stable`` is reserved
    by Debian/Ubuntu for actual stable releases.

 -- Laurent Lavaud <l.lavaud@gmail.com>  Tue, 19 May 2026 23:32:00 +0200

process-media (2.0.1-1) stable; urgency=medium

  * Recognise common date patterns in file names when EXIF metadata is
    missing (Samsung ``YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS``, iPhone ``IMG_…``,
    ``Screenshot_YYYY-MM-DD-HH-MM-SS``, WhatsApp ``IMG-YYYYMMDD-…``)
    so screenshots and PNG captures are renamed consistently with
    EXIF-tagged photos.
  * Always log how the base name was resolved (EXIF tag used, date
    parsed from the filename, or fallback to the original stem with
    a warning) so users can immediately understand why a given file
    was or was not renamed to YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS.
  * Add ``.png`` to the recognised photo extensions.

 -- Laurent Lavaud <l.lavaud@gmail.com>  Tue, 19 May 2026 23:30:37 +0200

process-media (2.0.0-1) stable; urgency=medium

  * Initial Debian package for the Python rewrite (2.0.0).
    - Drop the legacy Perl implementation in favour of a Python 3.11+
      package built with hatchling.
    - Drop the ``pyexiftool`` Python dependency in favour of calling the
      ``exiftool`` binary directly, keeping the dependency footprint
      aligned with what Debian stable / Ubuntu LTS ship out of the box.
    - Switch the project license to MIT.

 -- Laurent Lavaud <l.lavaud@gmail.com>  Tue, 19 May 2026 22:36:35 +0200
